==Strategy==
It is highly recommended to have all of the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures|anti-Starred Alien]] [[Treasure]]s before even attempting this stage. Even missing a single Treasure can increase the already high difficulty to crazy levels. For your lineup, you generally want three [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]], consisting of [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|dual]] [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Erasers]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]. You also want to bring a good [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]], an obvious choice being [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]]. Attacker-wise, you will want [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] (only if you want to do extra damage to Bun Bun Symbiote), and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]. For your remaining slots, fill them in with good [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] or a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] unit like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] or [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] to keep the Corporal Weylands in check. [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|Nukers]] are also extremely effective here if you can get enough money to afford them, so keep that in mind.

During the battle, you want to make sure you conserve your money as much as possible while also trying to keep the Corporal Weylands from destroying your stack. There is an element of luck from Bun Bun Symbiote's [[Wave Attack]]s, but those can be nullified if you bring [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or another [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] unit like [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]]. Focus on defeating the Corporal Weylands while [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controlling]] the Imperator Saels and Bun Bun Symbiote and victory will be yours.

